{"title":"2005 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 17","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_17&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>How many distinct four-tuples <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/e/faedb9d30dc3763d92cbcacf2cc17e2bf64f3e8b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a,b,c,d)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"75\" height=\"20\" /> of rational numbers are there with\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/1/5/9153c41adf40f93e619e0362b706aa5160874e9c.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[a\\cdot\\log_{10}2+b\\cdot\\log_{10}3+c\\cdot\\log_{10}5+d\\cdot\\log_{10}7=2005?\\]\" width=\"420\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/8/638923196694a77c65e56e84d8b691cb2f77b29f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathrm{(A)}\\ 0      \\qquad \\mathrm{(B)}\\ 1      \\qquad \\mathrm{(C)}\\ 17     \\qquad \\mathrm{(D)}\\ 2004   \\qquad \\mathrm{(E)}\\ \\text{infinitely many}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"479\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_17&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Using the laws of <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Logarithms\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Logarithms\">logarithms</a>, the given equation becomes\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/b/3/9b367a566b912c5625212b4998ae7e4acb4a4918.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\log_{10}2^{a}+\\log_{10}3^{b}+\\log_{10}5^{c}+\\log_{10}7^{d}=2005\\]\" width=\"353\" height=\"20\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/b/34b1fdf053c6b026b0976f3f18c9a30db5ee001a.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\Rightarrow \\log_{10}{2^{a}\\cdot 3^{b}\\cdot 5^{c}\\cdot 7^{d}}=2005\\]\" width=\"228\" height=\"20\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/9/859b1435302b7be43757fbe0695894a5fc73e38b.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\Rightarrow 2^{a}\\cdot 3^{b}\\cdot 5^{c}\\cdot 7^{d} = 10^{2005}\\]\" width=\"195\" height=\"16\" />\n</p><p>As <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/6/bb60e0857a2c0a2c47acfbe81781032feb1f7150.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a,b,c,d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" /> must all be rational, and there are no powers of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/a/e0a0db32027a732ac57d37ef2ae9bb150f65b108.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/8/6/5865c4fb44f1c6ccbe8ceb7773bed0e3a0aa3645.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10^{2005}$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"43\" height=\"15\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/7/ed7de3fc50cca2e447f373e6f9430665852d75b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b=d=0$\" width=\"74\" height=\"12\" />. Then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/1/061bffb6b21bca10d27f69fa9589dbd10f0faf62.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^{a}\\cdot 5^{c}=2^{2005}\\cdot 5^{2005} \\Rightarrow a=c=2005$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"286\" height=\"15\" />.\n</p><p>Only the four-tuple <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/b/c/ebc95cf85705799c5dd7af9ecd82cbacfe2d3622.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(2005,0,2005,0)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"127\" height=\"18\" /> satisfies the equation, so the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/1/961f5ccad482b5aee0ddc944b076c23e97ea8c2e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{1} \\Rightarrow \\mathrm{(B)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"74\" height=\"23\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_17&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"2\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_12B\" title=\"2005 AMC 12B\">2005 AMC 12B</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_12B_Problems\" title=\"2005 AMC 12B Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_12B_Answer_Key\" title=\"2005 AMC 12B Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_16\" title=\"2005 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 16\">Problem 16</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_18\" title=\"2005 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 18\">Problem 18</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"2\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2005 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2005 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?t